{
  "abstract": "For each complex terminal two-plane in dimension five, two real orthonormal terminal frames preserve all five coordinate weights and bracket the compressed two-step Hardy success for every positive Schmidt spectrum. The same two frames work throughout this family of spectra. For spectra proportional to (s,2,3,4,5) with 0<s≤2, the exact maximum at unrestricted endpoint ranks is attained by the real pairs (2,4) and (3,5).",
